{"tool_name":"pazar","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pazar","home":"http://www.pazar.info/","summary":"Open access and open source database of transcription factor and regulatory sequence annotation with associated web interface and programming tools designed to submit and query data related to the regulation of gene expression.","addition_date":"2017-04-25T12:30:08Z","last_update_date":"2021-04-26T08:51:47Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:pazar","credit":[{"email":"pazar@cmmt.ubc.ca","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.pazar.info/cgi-bin/help_FAQ.pl"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"},{"term":"Query and retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0224"},{"term":"Transcriptional regulatory element prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0438"}]}],"name":"PAZAR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"PAZAR is an open-access and open-source database of transcription factor and regulatory sequence annotation with associated web interface and programming tools for data submission and extraction. Curated boutique data collections can be maintained and disseminated through the unified schema of the mall-like PAZAR repository. The Pleiades Promoter Project collection of brain-linked regulatory sequences is introduced to demonstrate the depth of annotation possible within PAZAR. PAZAR, located at http://www.pazar.info, is open for business. \u00a9 2007 Portales-Casamar et al.; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.","authors":[{"name":"Kirov S."},{"name":"Lim J."},{"name":"Lithwick S."},{"name":"Portales-Casamar E."},{"name":"Snoddy J."},{"name":"Swanson M.I."},{"name":"Ticoll A."},{"name":"Wasserman W.W."}],"citationCount":69,"date":"2007-09-28T00:00:00Z","journal"